    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d572">

                <pb facs="0556" n="480" xml:id="pg480"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/17367</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Special Agent Carothers
                        to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">El Paso</hi></placeName>, [<date
                            ana="#date_undated-inferred-from-document-content" calendar="gregorian"
                            notAfter="1916-03-08T23:59:59-05:00"
                            notBefore="1916-03-01T00:00:00-07:00"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >undated</hi></date><hi rendition="#italic">; received March 8,
                            1916</hi>.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>General Villa is reported to be at Nogales Ranch, about 25 miles from border and
                    65 miles from Hachita, New Mexico. Indications are that he is going west into
                    Sonora.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Carothers</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
